  "term": "social desirability",
  "definition": "Social desirability is a personality trait involving qualities that make a person seem acceptable or appealing in social and interpersonal relationships. It is linked with being socially approved of or accepted, and with attributes such as popularity, social standing, or leadership that make someone a preferred companion.",
